abstract: >
  NeuroBloom is an open-source research software prototype for studying
  longitudinal cognitive-task records and clinician-supervised rehabilitation
  workflows in multiple sclerosis. It provides adaptive cognitive tasks,
  descriptive longitudinal indicators, clinician review, and bilingual
  (English/Bengali) support. The psychometric and clinical validity of its
  task implementations and analytics has not been established.

keywords:
  - multiple sclerosis
  - digital health
